# `a2a docs`: the embedded documentation corpus, printed by topic (P9,
# answers-that-hold-2026-08).
#
# What THIS row buys, and it is the criterion the phase is judged at: spec 09's
# AC-1 and AC-6 both name "a declared path running the built binary in an empty
# directory", and until this file existed that tier was discharged by hand
# once, by the lead, in a scratch directory. The in-process tests
# (internal/cli/cmd_docs_test.go, internal/mcp/tools_docs_test.go) prove the
# vocabulary derivation, the refusals and the missing-page case against
# fixture manifests. They cannot prove the verb is ROUTED, or that it needs
# nothing from the working directory it is standing in.
#
# The txtar cwd is a fresh empty directory with no .a2a/ at all. That is not
# incidental setup — it IS the assertion. The verb reads bytes embedded in the
# binary and touches nothing else, which is why the agent this verb exists for
# (working inside another team's repository, with no a2ahub checkout) can call
# it at all.

# 1. Bare invocation lists the vocabulary, grouped in manifest group order,
#    and exits 0 with no project, no space and no working tree.
exec a2a docs
stdout 'Start:'
stdout 'getting-started'
stdout 'Concepts:'
stdout 'work-loops'

# 2. A named topic prints that section's page.
exec a2a docs work-loops
stdout 'loops'

# 3. An unknown topic REFUSES and names the vocabulary it actually holds,
#    rather than telling the reader to go and find the docs — the whole point
#    being that they could not find them, which is why they are here.
! exec a2a docs no-such-topic
stderr 'no such topic'
stderr 'getting-started'
stderr 'work-loops'

# local-space-2026-10 spec 06 §8. Each stanza below prints a page through the
# built binary, from this same empty directory, and asserts the local-space
# text an agent acts on.

# AC1 (getting-started-local-space): the onboarding page carries the local
# path, in P3's grammar, with the `local:` owner form and no credential. That
# the section instructs no `gh` and no pull request is asserted in process
# (internal/cli/cmd_doctor_docs_test.go), where the section can be cut out.
exec a2a docs getting-started
stdout '## Local space — one operator, several repositories'
stdout 'a2a space init <space-id> --local'
stdout 'a2a connect <path>'
stdout 'local:<system>'
stdout 'no credential'

# AC2 (loop-express-topic): the express loop is its own page, naming the three
# composite verbs, with --record on the verify step.
exec a2a docs loop-express
stdout 'a2a data request'
stdout 'a2a data deliver --for'
stdout 'a2a data verify --for <XW-id> --record'

# AC3 (work-loops-routes-express): the routing table sends an express space's
# data exchange to that page, and names `flow` as what selects it.
exec a2a docs work-loops
stdout '\[Express data loop\]\(loops/express.md\)'
stdout 'whose `flow` is `express`'

# AC4 (session-start-names-mode-read): a numbered session-start step, outside
# the quoted plan block (whose lines start with "> "), tells the agent to read
# the mode once and names the three fields.
stdout '^8\. \*\*Read each space''s mode\.\*\* Run `a2a version --json`'
stdout '`flow`'
stdout '`gates`'
stdout '`lands_synchronously`'

# AC8 (work-loops-gates-qualifier): the human-gate paragraph says a confirm
# local space refuses a gated write without --approve, and that --approve is
# passed only on the human's word.
stdout 'refuses a G1–G4 write without `--approve`'
stdout 'only on your human''s word'

# AC9 (loop-send-await-local): `a2a await` has nothing to wait for on a host
# that lands writes synchronously.
exec a2a docs loop-send
stdout 'nothing to wait for'

# AC10 (identity-and-exchange-local-qualifiers).
exec a2a docs actor-identity
stdout 'owner string `local:<system>`'
exec a2a docs data-exchange
stdout 'the merge-before-response hazard does not arise'

# AC6 (troubleshooting-local-rows): the three local-only resolution rows. The
# "Common resolutions" table moved to its own page before this phase (spec 06
# §11, from the wave-4 lane), so the topic is `resolutions`.
exec a2a docs resolutions
stdout 'refusing refs/heads/main: this local space lands writes only through a2a'
stdout 'land contended'
stdout 'space: prepared-target-stale'
